Scrolls for which a spellbook exists:
 * Identify
 * Remove curse
 * Magic mapping
 * Taming (charm monster)
 * Food detection (detect food)
 * Create monster
 * Scare monster (cause fear)
Wands for which a spellbook exists:
 * Cold (cone of cold)
 * Magic missile
 * Striking (force bolt)
 * Death (finger of death)
 * Secret door detection (detect unseen)
 * Slow monster
 * Light
 * Teleportation (teleport away)
 * Cancellation
 * Digging (dig)
 * Sleep
 * Opening (knock)
 * Locking (wizard lock)
 * Undead turning (turn undead)
 * Polymorph
Potions for which a spellbook exists:
 * Object detection (detect treasure)
 * Speed (haste self)
 * Monster detection (detect monsters)
 * Restore ability
 * Invisibility
Spells which do not exactly coincide with any potion, wand, or scroll:
 * Healing/Extra healing (do not cure afflictions)
 * Cure blindness/sickness (cure only their stated affliction)
 * Protection
 * Jumping
 * Stone to flesh
 * Create familiar
 * Clairvoyance
 * Fireball

Many of the coincidences are not exact - often the spell has extended
capabilities, and of course the direct-damage spells end up being much
more powerful than the wands they are based on.

So, which of the spells that duplicate other items would you cut?
(Cancellation is, I suppose, an obvious choice.)
